Kaen probably *is* more dangerous than Rodney if you have magic resistance.
His physical attacks do really quite a lot of damage (two lots of
16-32), and if you haven't got either magic resistance or free action,
you're pretty much doomed.  He's a clerical spellcaster, so can cast
paralyze.  Also, he's immune to stoning, which Rodney *isn't*.

(Yeah, Rodney can score a true instakill on characters without MR, but
everyone knows you need MR to take on Gehennom safely.  If you're mostly
used to playing Valkyries, Kaen comes as a *very* nasty shock - he's got
more hit points and more damage potential than any of the other quest
nemeses.)

